title CGT Phase 2: Emergent Core Category Discovery

Container(Main_Concern_Sensor, "Main Concern Sensor", "Problem Detector", "Senses latent main concern")

Container(Core_Emergence_Detector, "Core Emergence Detector", "Pattern Integrator", "Detects emergent core")

Container(Interchangeability_Tester, "Interchangeability Tester", "Concept Validator", "Tests true interchangeability")

== Phase 2: Letting Core Emerge ==

note over Main_Concern_Sensor, Core_Emergence_Detector

**CGT PRINCIPLE: Let It Emerge**

No external theory comparison

No forcing of categories

Let patterns reveal themselves

end note

group Main Concern Discovery (Natural)

Main_Concern_Sensor -> Code_Tracker: Review all codes

Main_Concern_Sensor -> Memo_Bank: Review memos

Main_Concern_Sensor -> Main_Concern_Sensor: Sense latent concern

note right

**LATENT CONCERN SENSING:**

1. What problems recur in codes?

2. What tensions appear in memos?

3. What drives participant behavior?

4. Don't look for stated problems

5. Sense the underlying worry

end note

Main_Concern_Sensor -> Orchestrator: "Main concern sensed: [Concern]"

end

group Core Category Emergence (Natural)

Core_Emergence_Detector -> Code_Tracker: Review pattern landscape

Core_Emergence_Detector -> Core_Emergence_Detector: Let core reveal itself

note right

**CORE REVELATION PROCESS:**

Questions to ask (not algorithms):

1. Which pattern resolves the main concern?

2. Which pattern connects to most others?

3. Which pattern has theoretical grab?

4. Which pattern feels central?

No scoring, no algorithms

Qualitative, emergent sense

end note

Core_Emergence_Detector -> Interchangeability_Tester: "Test candidate: [Pattern]"

end

group True Interchangeability Testing

Interchangeability_Tester -> Code_Tracker: Get incidents for pattern

Interchangeability_Tester -> Interchangeability_Tester: Test conceptual equivalence

note right

**INTERCHANGEABILITY TEST:**

Take 3 different incidents with same code:

1. Strip away context details

2. Compare core process essence

3. Ask: "Are these really the same?"

4. Test: Can they substitute in explanation?

If yes → category valid

If no → refine or split category

end note

alt True interchangeability

Interchangeability_Tester -> Core_Emergence_Detector: "Valid category"

else Not interchangeable

Interchangeability_Tester -> Code_Tracker: "Split or refine category"

end

end

group Natural Delimitation

Core_Emergence_Detector -> Orchestrator: "Core emerged: [Core Category]"

Orchestrator -> All_Agents: "Switch to selective coding"

note right of Orchestrator

**NATURAL DELIMITATION:**

1. Now focus only on core

2. Code only related data

3. Ignore interesting but irrelevant

4. Let comparison continue naturally

end note

end

