title CGT Phase 3: Selective Coding with True Saturation

Container(Selective_Coder, "Selective Coder", "Focused Analyst", "Codes only core-related data")

Container(True_Saturation_Detector, "True Saturation Detector", "Interchangeability Monitor", "Monitors conceptual saturation")

Container(Theoretical_Sampler, "Theoretical Sampler", "Gap Filler", "Samples for specific gaps")

== Phase 3: Natural Selective Coding ==

note over Selective_Coder, Theoretical_Sampler

**CGT REALITY: Field-Based Sampling**

Primarily sample from available data

Only use external sources when necessary

Focus on filling specific theoretical gaps

end note

group Selective Coding Process

loop For each new segment

Selective_Coder -> Transcript_DB: Fetch segment

Selective_Coder -> Selective_Coder: Assess relevance naturally

note right

**NATURAL RELEVANCE ASSESSMENT:**

1. Does this relate to core category?

2. Does it develop core properties?

3. If yes → code it

4. If no → ignore it (delimitation)

No scoring algorithms

Natural judgment based on understanding

end note

alt Relevant to core

Selective_Coder -> Code_Tracker: "Develop property: [Property]"

True_Saturation_Detector -> Code_Tracker: Monitor development

end

end

end

group True Saturation via Interchangeability

True_Saturation_Detector -> True_Saturation_Detector: Check saturation

note right

**TRUE SATURATION DEFINITION:**

Saturation occurs when:

New incidents add NO NEW PROPERTIES

to existing categories.

All indicators become interchangeable.

Not about counting incidents.

About conceptual completeness.

end note

loop Until saturation

True_Saturation_Detector -> Code_Tracker: Get latest incidents

True_Saturation_Detector -> True_Saturation_Detector: Check for new properties

note right

**NEW PROPERTY CHECK:**

For each new incident:

1. Does it reveal new dimension of category?

2. New condition for occurrence?

3. New consequence?

4. New strategy variation?

If no new properties in last 5 incidents → saturated

end note

alt No new properties (interchangeability achieved)

True_Saturation_Detector -> Orchestrator: "Conceptually saturated"

break

else New property discovered

True_Saturation_Detector -> Theoretical_Sampler: "Gap: [Specific property gap]"

end

end

end

group Natural Theoretical Sampling

Theoretical_Sampler -> True_Saturation_Detector: Receive gap information

Theoretical_Sampler -> Theoretical_Sampler: Plan natural sampling

note right

**NATURAL SAMPLING APPROACH:**

1. Look for data that might fill this gap

2. Search existing transcripts first

3. Only if necessary: look externally

4. External sources = new data to code

Example gap: "How does core occur in conflict?"

→ Look for conflict situations in transcripts

→ If none, maybe search conflict literature (as new data)

end note

alt Gap requires existing data

Theoretical_Sampler -> Transcript_DB: "Find segments about: [Gap topic]"

else Gap requires external knowledge

Theoretical_Sampler -> External_Sources: "Search as NEW data about: [Gap]"

External_Sources -> Transcript_DB: Store as new transcript

note right of Transcript_DB

**EXTERNAL AS NEW DATA:**

Literature excerpts treated as:

• New "interviews" to code

• Compare to existing theory

• Not as authority to follow

end note

end

end

